  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Minor in Entrepreneurship and Innovation"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Minors",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Minors",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/minors/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Students who complete the Entrepreneurship and Innovation Minor will have developed an understanding of the process of entrepreneurship and the essential factors needed for the successful growth of a new venture. Also, students will have developed an appreciation for the challenges involved in managing innovation and in nurturing creative thinking."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Administered by: Ted Rogers School of Business Management, Entrepreneurship & Strategy Department"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Exclusions: This minor is not available to students in the following programs:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Business Management - Entrepreneurship and Innovation Major",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Business Management - Entrepreneurship and Innovation Major",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/programs/trsm/business_mgt/entrepreneurship_major/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "To receive this Minor, students must complete six (6) courses from the following curriculum:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Two (2) Required courses:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "ENT 526 Entrepreneurial Behaviour and Strategy or ENT 524 The Practice of Entrepreneurship",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "ENT 526",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/entrepreneurship-and-strategy/ENT/526/"
        },
        {
          "text": "ENT 524",
